# NovelGuard Architecture

Full detail: [docs/current_architecture.md](mdc:docs/current_architecture.md).

## Layers

| Layer | Path | Principle |
|-------|------|-----------|
| domain | `src/domain/` | Pure rules, value objects, policies |
| application | `src/application/` | Use cases, DTOs, ports |
| infrastructure | `src/infrastructure/` | DB, FS, hashing; map to DTOs |
| ui | `web/` | React + Tailwind UI; calls application via API/ports only |
| app | `src/app/` | Composition and wiring |
| tests | `tests/` | Unit, integration, golden |

## Dependency Direction

- `domain` imports no other project layers.
- `application` depends on `domain` and `application.ports` only.
- `infrastructure` implements ports and hides external libraries.
- `web/` depends on application DTOs/API contracts, not concrete infrastructure.
- `app` wires infrastructure, GUI, and use cases.

## Ports

- Ports live in `src/application/ports/`.
- Use cases depend on port protocols, not concrete classes.
- Port changes belong in application.
- Infrastructure implementations stay in infrastructure.
- Domain rules stay in domain.

## Domain Terms

- **FileEntry:** scanned file immutable facts: path, size, mtime, extension.
- **FilenameParseResult:** parsed title, range, and tags from filename.
- **DuplicateGroupResult:** group verdict: file IDs, keeper, confidence, evidence.

## Do Not

- No I/O, UI, DB, or external API in `domain`.
- No concrete infrastructure imports in `application`.
- No business policy in `infrastructure`.
